 "notes": "The two pits at Strandpark Slijk-Ewijk in the Waal floodplain: the south lake (Gat van Hage, to about 33-36 m) entered from the beach, and the Noordplas entered over a grass bank from the same car park; shorelines, piers and beaches from OpenStreetMap (© OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL), entry positions from duikbuddygezocht.nl. The site is named only 'Slijk-Ewijk', so both entries are drawn. Duikplaats.net describes walls west of the beach entry (shoreline on the right) and a wreck in the south lake, and reeds, clay blocks from 5 m and jagged clay walls west of the Noordplas entry; the wall markers are placed only by that direction and the wreck's position is not known, so it is left out. The site coordinates are the village of Slijk-Ewijk, about 1.2 km south-east of the lakes.",
